resources.string:
In NearHouse, it is prohibited to:
• publish false or misleading information;
• upload offensive content;
• commit or attempt fraud;
• impersonate another person;
• publish a property without authorization from its owner.
All listings undergo review by an administrator before being published. Photos must be taken at the property.

We only collect data that NearHouse needs to operate.

To create your account:
• full name;
• email;
• phone number;
• password;
• date of birth.

If you sign in with Google: the name and email of your Google account.

Data you add:
• profile photo;
• listings with their photos;
• address and location of the property;
• contact info for your listings (name, phone, and email);
• saved listings.

Location: we use your device's location when taking photos for a listing and when using the map. We only use it at those times.

Camera: we use it only for you to take photos of the property.

Payments: when paying for a listing or choosing a plan, the app shows an example payment form. Payments are simulated: no charge is made, and we do not send or store your card details. We recommend not entering real card details.

When you publish a listing, other users can see:
• its photos;
• the address and location of the property;
• your contact info: name, phone, and email.

If you do not want other people to see this information, do not publish listings.
